cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  HIPO conformation model — tautomer-encoded directional conformational
  control in imidazopyridine oligomers
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this record) and
  the accompanying paper listed under `references`.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Octavio
    family-names: Miranda
    affiliation: Department of Chemistry, Texas A&M University
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1478-1560'
version: 1.5.0
date-released: '2026-08-10'
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A probabilistic model of backbone conformation in regioregular
  hydrogen-bonded imidazopyridine oligomers (HIPO). Each bridging bond is
  treated as a dimer carrying a tautomeric state and a torsion angle;
  because adjacent dimers share a monomer, tautomer compatibility between
  overlapping dimers acts as a transition matrix. DFT-derived conditional
  distributions P(phi|T) are propagated along the chain by Bayesian belief
  propagation, giving pairwise and cumulative torsional joint distributions,
  tautomer profiles, and cis/trans profiles at arbitrary chain length.
keywords:
  - conjugated polymers
  - conformational analysis
  - tautomerism
  - belief propagation
  - rotational isomeric state
  - hydrogen bonding
  - density functional theory
repository-code: 'https://github.com/octaviomirandaphd/hipo-conformation-model'
# Concept DOI — always resolves to the newest version. Cite this one in the paper.
# (The v1.0.0 version DOI is 10.5281/zenodo.21755593; v1.1.0 will mint its own.)
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21755592
